WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:01.497
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:02.731
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.731 --> 00:00:04.739
My one word is believe and I believe that

00:00:04.739 --> 00:00:06.718
entrepreneurs will
solve all of the world's

00:00:06.718 --> 00:00:08.049
major problems.

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:09.774
So to help you on your journey, today's

00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:12.800
message is, motivation is garbage.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.687
Over to you, Mel Robbins.

00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:17.122
(rooster crowing)

00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:19.482
♫ I wake up every morning,

00:00:19.482 --> 00:00:21.846
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:25.429
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:30.139
- We bought into this
complete falsehood that

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:33.314
at some point you're
going to have the courage.

00:00:33.314 --> 00:00:35.281
At some point you're going
to have the confidence.

00:00:35.281 --> 00:00:36.584
And it's total bull, frankly.

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:37.903
Are we allowed to swear on this show?

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:38.736
- Absolutely.

00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:39.569
- Okay.

00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:40.830
It's complete garbage.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.723
And so there are so many
people in the world,

00:00:43.723 --> 00:00:47.404
and you may be watching
this right now, and

00:00:47.404 --> 00:00:50.331
you have these incredible
ideas and what you

00:00:50.331 --> 00:00:52.535
think is missing is motivation.

00:00:52.535 --> 00:00:53.897
And that's not true.

00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:56.772
Because the way that our minds are wired,

00:00:56.772 --> 00:00:59.474
and the fact about human beings is that we

00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:03.564
are not designed to do
things that are uncomfortable

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:05.554
or scary or difficult.

00:01:05.554 --> 00:01:09.307
Our brains are designed to
protect us from those things.

00:01:09.307 --> 00:01:11.531
Because our brains are
trying to keep us alive.

00:01:11.531 --> 00:01:14.341
And in order to change, in
order to build a business,

00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:16.940
in order to be the best
parent, the best spouse, to

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.091
do all those things that
you know you want to do

00:01:20.091 --> 00:01:21.976
with your life, with your
work, with your dreams,

00:01:21.976 --> 00:01:25.297
you're going to have to do
things that are difficult,

00:01:25.297 --> 00:01:28.924
uncertain or scary, which
sets up this problem

00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:30.655
for all of us.

00:01:30.655 --> 00:01:32.160
You're never going to feel like it.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.562
Motivation is garbage.

00:01:33.562 --> 00:01:36.291
You only feel motivated
to do the things that

00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:37.624
are easy, right?

00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:40.333
- Why do you think that is?

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.869
- Oh, I know exactly why that is.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:44.943
Because I've studied this
so much, because for me,

00:01:44.943 --> 00:01:47.720
one of the hardest
things to figure out was

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.970
why is it so hard to do the

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.543
little things that would improve my life?

00:01:55.543 --> 00:01:58.378
And what I've come to
realize and what we'll talk

00:01:58.378 --> 00:02:01.427
a lot about today is that
the way that our minds

00:02:01.427 --> 00:02:05.795
are designed, is our minds
are designed to stop you

00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:09.962
at all costs from doing
anything that might hurt you.

00:02:11.751 --> 00:02:15.718
And the way that this all
happens is, it all starts

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:19.885
with something super subtle
that none of us ever catch,

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:23.334
and that is with this
habit that all of us have

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.269
that nobody's talking about.

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:28.102
We all have a habit of hesitating.

00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:31.011
We have an idea.

00:02:31.011 --> 00:02:32.627
You're sitting in a meeting.

00:02:32.627 --> 00:02:34.390
You have this incredible idea.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:38.320
And instead of just
saying it, you stop and

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.628
you hesitate.

00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:41.452
Now, what none of us
realize is that when you

00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:43.846
hesitate just that
moment, that micro-moment,

00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:46.592
that small hesitation,
it sends a stress signal

00:02:46.592 --> 00:02:48.017
to your brain.

00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:49.792
It wakes your brain up and
your brain all of a sudden

00:02:49.792 --> 00:02:51.599
goes oh, wait a minute.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:52.650
Why is he hesitating?

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.311
He didn't hesitate when
he put on his killer

00:02:54.311 --> 00:02:55.295
spiky sneakers.

00:02:55.295 --> 00:02:57.741
He didn't hesitate with the
really cool track pants.

00:02:57.741 --> 00:02:59.369
He didn't hesitate with the NASA t-shirt.

00:02:59.369 --> 00:03:01.731
Now he's hesitating to
talk, something must be up.

00:03:01.731 --> 00:03:04.435
So then your brain goes
to work to protect you.

00:03:04.435 --> 00:03:07.039
It has a million different
ways to protect you.

00:03:07.039 --> 00:03:08.585
One of them is called
the spotlight effect.

00:03:08.585 --> 00:03:11.815
It's a known phenomenon where
your brain magnifies risk.

00:03:11.815 --> 00:03:12.648
Why?

00:03:12.648 --> 00:03:14.579
To pull you away from
something that it perceives

00:03:14.579 --> 00:03:16.187
to be a problem.

00:03:16.187 --> 00:03:21.129
And so you can truly trace
every single problem or

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:25.466
complaint in your life to
silence and hesitation.

00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:26.723
Those are decisions.

00:03:26.723 --> 00:03:30.400
And what I do and what's
changed my life is

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.958
waking up and realizing
that motivation is garbage.

00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:35.259
I'm never going to feel
like doing the things that

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:37.872
are tough or difficult or
uncertain or scary or new.

00:03:37.872 --> 00:03:40.829
So I need to stop waiting
until I feel like it.

00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:43.878
And number two, I am
one decision away from

00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:46.875
a totally different marriage,
a totally different life,

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:49.775
a totally different job, a
totally different income,

00:03:49.775 --> 00:03:53.924
a totally different
relationship with my kids.

00:03:53.924 --> 00:03:57.250
Not like one decision, I'm divorcing you,

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.828
in the marriage example.

00:03:58.828 --> 00:04:01.901
But one decision on, you could be having a

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.989
conversation with your spouse and you feel

00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:08.382
your emotions rise up
and within a tiny window

00:04:08.382 --> 00:04:11.965
those emotions can take
over and can impact

00:04:12.876 --> 00:04:14.510
how your marriage goes.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.187
Or, you can learn how
to take control of that

00:04:18.187 --> 00:04:22.413
micro-moment and make a
decision to act in a way

00:04:22.413 --> 00:04:24.375
that actually shifts your marriage.

00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:26.980
Your life comes down to
your decisions and if

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:30.430
you change your decisions,
you will change everything.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.142
- So I don't know that
I agree completely that

00:04:32.142 --> 00:04:33.762
motivation is absolute garbage.

00:04:33.762 --> 00:04:35.357
I've seen motivation work for me.

00:04:35.357 --> 00:04:37.895
I've put on a Tony
Robbins CD and then want

00:04:37.895 --> 00:04:39.939
to go off and do amazing things and I did.

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:40.792
I took action.

00:04:40.792 --> 00:04:42.745
I took all my gear and
I went out and would

00:04:42.745 --> 00:04:44.760
do something that I
was afraid of doing and

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.996
I took action on it.

00:04:45.996 --> 00:04:47.199
So I know that it can work.

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:49.480
The challenge is, we
don't have Tony Robbins

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.825
chasing around us all the time telling us

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:53.160
to go and do something.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.601
And that kind of
motivation is super short.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:59.923
I don't wake up every
day, life is amazing,

00:04:59.923 --> 00:05:02.022
I can't wait to go crush
it, this is insane.

00:05:02.022 --> 00:05:04.967
And so that kind of
motivation comes in bursts

00:05:04.967 --> 00:05:07.625
and I think can be
helpful, but it's hard to

00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:10.288
keep a consistent and
practical and ongoing basis.

00:05:10.288 --> 00:05:12.371
Because even if I listen
to that CD again or

00:05:12.371 --> 00:05:14.652
even if I watch that
video again, it starts to

00:05:14.652 --> 00:05:15.813
lose its impact.

00:05:15.813 --> 00:05:18.605
If you watch the same video
over and over and over

00:05:18.605 --> 00:05:21.439
again, the first time it
might be really motivating.

00:05:21.439 --> 00:05:23.217
It might make you go do something.

00:05:23.217 --> 00:05:24.489
And then you watch it
again and the impact's

00:05:24.489 --> 00:05:26.782
not there, and the third,
fourth, by the time you

00:05:26.782 --> 00:05:28.057
get to the fifth, sixth,
seventh, eighth, ninth,

00:05:28.057 --> 00:05:31.162
tenth time, it's like yeah,
I've heard that message before.

00:05:31.162 --> 00:05:31.995
You know, I've heard that.

00:05:31.995 --> 00:05:33.064
And it's not motivating anymore.

00:05:33.064 --> 00:05:34.888
And so that's why it's
really hard to keep that

00:05:34.888 --> 00:05:37.032
external motivation going.

00:05:37.032 --> 00:05:39.379
I think what's much more
practical, at least for me

00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:42.176
I've seen it work consistently
in my life, is one,

00:05:42.176 --> 00:05:44.868
having an environment that
is designed to help you

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:45.933
be more successful.

00:05:45.933 --> 00:05:47.619
So figure out what you
want and where it is.

00:05:47.619 --> 00:05:48.696
Mine is believe.

00:05:48.696 --> 00:05:50.824
I want to have an environment
that makes me believe

00:05:50.824 --> 00:05:52.817
in myself and the great
things that I'm trying to do

00:05:52.817 --> 00:05:54.955
on a daily basis, on a consistent basis.

00:05:54.955 --> 00:05:57.422
The habits that you have
on a consistent basis,

00:05:57.422 --> 00:05:59.432
the people that you
surround yourself with,

00:05:59.432 --> 00:06:01.682
the media that you consume,
the books that you read,

00:06:01.682 --> 00:06:04.232
your physical environment, it all matters.

00:06:04.232 --> 00:06:06.583
It all has an impact, every single day.

00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:09.468
And the confidence that
I've gained over the past

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:11.843
few years and how much
of this come out on the

00:06:11.843 --> 00:06:15.138
videos that I've made
for you guys, is in great

00:06:15.138 --> 00:06:17.462
part due to the videos that I've watched,

00:06:17.462 --> 00:06:18.769
the videos on my channel.

00:06:18.769 --> 00:06:20.683
By surrounding myself consistently with

00:06:20.683 --> 00:06:22.506
successful people.

00:06:22.506 --> 00:06:24.805
Not just entrepreneurs, people.

00:06:24.805 --> 00:06:26.391
The way they act, the things they say,

00:06:26.391 --> 00:06:28.930
their mindset, the way
they interpret information.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.573
The patterns start to
consistently come in,

00:06:31.573 --> 00:06:33.441
over and over and over
again, whether it's a

00:06:33.441 --> 00:06:35.044
Michael Jordan or a Mel Robbins or an

00:06:35.044 --> 00:06:37.616
Arnold Schwarzenegger or
Bill Gates or Tony Robbins

00:06:37.616 --> 00:06:38.609
or whoever it is.

00:06:38.609 --> 00:06:40.747
You start to see that these people think

00:06:40.747 --> 00:06:42.166
in a certain way.

00:06:42.166 --> 00:06:43.759
And the more you see
it, not just what they

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:45.841
say to do, not just do this step,

00:06:45.841 --> 00:06:48.417
but how they do it, how
they react to questions,

00:06:48.417 --> 00:06:49.924
being around them.

00:06:49.924 --> 00:06:51.786
Because I can't be
around Steve Jobs, right?

00:06:51.786 --> 00:06:52.619
He passed away.

00:06:52.619 --> 00:06:54.232
I'm not going to go visit his grave.

00:06:54.232 --> 00:06:55.687
I can't be around him anymore.

00:06:55.687 --> 00:06:57.122
But I can with the videos.

00:06:57.122 --> 00:06:58.318
At least it works well for me.

00:06:58.318 --> 00:07:00.284
And the more I'm around that, the more it

00:07:00.284 --> 00:07:02.641
makes me want to raise up my game.

00:07:02.641 --> 00:07:04.247
The more it makes me feel like I want to

00:07:04.247 --> 00:07:06.101
go off and do bigger things.

00:07:06.101 --> 00:07:08.728
And it's allowed me to have bolder goals,

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:11.423
to be more controversial,
to be more myself,

00:07:11.423 --> 00:07:14.098
to be more outgoing,
to chase bigger things,

00:07:14.098 --> 00:07:15.637
to challenge people more.

00:07:15.637 --> 00:07:18.230
I keep doing it, right?

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.995
And so I think the
environment that you have

00:07:19.995 --> 00:07:21.839
when you have the
self-awareness to know what

00:07:21.839 --> 00:07:23.437
your one word is and build
an environment around it

00:07:23.437 --> 00:07:26.614
and habits and routines
really is important.

00:07:26.614 --> 00:07:28.902
The second thing I would
say about motivation is,

00:07:28.902 --> 00:07:31.925
I like to do trade-offs
around short-term fear

00:07:31.925 --> 00:07:33.366
and long-term fear.

00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:36.813
And so the trick is catching the fear.

00:07:36.813 --> 00:07:38.344
And the trick is catching
yourself when you're in

00:07:38.344 --> 00:07:40.070
the moment, when you're
playing small, when

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.114
you're not doing the big
thing you should be doing,

00:07:42.114 --> 00:07:43.996
when you're just super
afraid and you disguise it

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.899
as some practical reason.

00:07:45.899 --> 00:07:47.869
You've convinced yourself
there's a logical reason

00:07:47.869 --> 00:07:49.594
why you're not doing it.

00:07:49.594 --> 00:07:51.767
We just naturally play
small when somebody asks

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:52.711
you to do things.

00:07:52.711 --> 00:07:54.467
Come on my YouTube channel and be a guest.

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:56.237
And most people are
like, oh, that's too big

00:07:56.237 --> 00:07:57.070
an opportunity.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:58.377
And I'm like, you have this opportunity!

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:03.123
And then they justify it with
all these reasons, right?

00:08:03.123 --> 00:08:04.340
I'm not ready.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.191
I don't have a good message.

00:08:06.191 --> 00:08:07.049
I don't have the gear.

00:08:07.049 --> 00:08:08.309
I don't have a webcam.

00:08:08.309 --> 00:08:09.796
I don't have a microphone.

00:08:09.796 --> 00:08:12.102
All of these reasons why
they can't do it but really,

00:08:12.102 --> 00:08:13.132
they're just afraid.

00:08:13.132 --> 00:08:15.431
That's the problem, they're just afraid.

00:08:15.431 --> 00:08:17.040
But it's catching the fear.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.120
They're not catching it.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.985
They're pushing it off with practicality

00:08:20.985 --> 00:08:22.033
but it's really fear.

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:24.317
And so I try to catch
that fear and then replace

00:08:24.317 --> 00:08:27.587
it with longer-term bigger fear.

00:08:27.587 --> 00:08:28.420
That's it.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.542
So this one thing that I'm afraid of doing

00:08:31.542 --> 00:08:34.563
versus one hundred years
old, looking back on my life,

00:08:34.563 --> 00:08:37.230
you know, sixty years of regret.

00:08:39.125 --> 00:08:40.750
That's scary.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.114
That's what I try to avoid.

00:08:42.114 --> 00:08:44.477
I tell this story about this girl in Paris

00:08:44.477 --> 00:08:48.012
that I met where I wanted to ask her out

00:08:48.012 --> 00:08:49.799
and I didn't and I was too afraid and

00:08:49.799 --> 00:08:51.927
I took a picture and I
didn't actually catch her

00:08:51.927 --> 00:08:53.164
in the picture, I tried.

00:08:53.164 --> 00:08:54.892
But I had this French
scenery that I put up

00:08:54.892 --> 00:08:58.150
on my wall at my university
room, because it was

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:02.534
a reminder not to let
opportunities pass by.

00:09:02.534 --> 00:09:06.275
But the next time that
I had an opportunity

00:09:06.275 --> 00:09:08.989
to ask somebody out, to
say yes to a business,

00:09:08.989 --> 00:09:11.707
to do whatever the thing
is I think in my head,

00:09:11.707 --> 00:09:12.689
that would be cool to do.

00:09:12.689 --> 00:09:14.218
But then the fear comes in.

00:09:14.218 --> 00:09:15.180
I'm going to take action.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.748
And looking at that poster
every day reminded me

00:09:17.748 --> 00:09:20.052
so that when I had that
opportunity to join

00:09:20.052 --> 00:09:22.729
a startup company a couple of months later

00:09:22.729 --> 00:09:26.344
versus taking the job that
I thought I always wanted,

00:09:26.344 --> 00:09:29.839
I had that picture in my head saying,

00:09:29.839 --> 00:09:31.484
this business may not work out.

00:09:31.484 --> 00:09:32.796
This startup company
that I'm about to join

00:09:32.796 --> 00:09:34.432
may not work out.

00:09:34.432 --> 00:09:36.748
Versus having this safe job that I thought

00:09:36.748 --> 00:09:40.031
I always wanted, paying
80 to $100,000 a year.

00:09:40.031 --> 00:09:42.327
But I didn't want to live with the regret.

00:09:42.327 --> 00:09:44.565
I didn't want to live with the regret.

00:09:44.565 --> 00:09:45.756
I could deal with the failure.

00:09:45.756 --> 00:09:47.390
I could deal with the pain
of it not working out.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.126
I could give it six
months or 12 months and if

00:09:49.126 --> 00:09:50.686
it doesn't work out, but I know.

00:09:50.686 --> 00:09:51.658
At least I know.

00:09:51.658 --> 00:09:54.188
I should have asked
that girl in France out.

00:09:54.188 --> 00:09:56.561
So at least I know, right?

00:09:56.561 --> 00:09:58.522
And ever since then
I've tried to make that

00:09:58.522 --> 00:10:01.566
same approach to important
decisions in my life.

00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:03.789
I try to ask myself,
yes, I'm afraid of this.

00:10:03.789 --> 00:10:05.368
If I can catch it, if
I can catch the fear,

00:10:05.368 --> 00:10:08.263
I'm afraid in the moment,
but if I don't do this,

00:10:08.263 --> 00:10:09.835
am I going to regret this
for the rest of my life?

00:10:09.835 --> 00:10:11.239
And if the answer is yes, then I know

00:10:11.239 --> 00:10:13.544
I have to do it and I
force myself to do it.

00:10:13.544 --> 00:10:14.377
And it works.

00:10:14.377 --> 00:10:15.439
At least, it works for me.

00:10:15.439 --> 00:10:16.281
So the question of the day to day is,

00:10:16.281 --> 00:10:18.406
I'm curious, what do
you think of motivation?

00:10:18.406 --> 00:10:19.239
How do you deal with?

00:10:19.239 --> 00:10:20.640
Does it help you long-term, short-term?

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.995
I'm very curious about your habits and

