00:10:58.637 --> 00:11:01.695
- Decision making is a process, right?

00:11:01.695 --> 00:11:03.625
The question is, what
filters are you using

00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:04.749
to make decisions.

00:11:04.749 --> 00:11:06.599
Are you making decisions
based on the financial

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:08.653
rewards or are you making decisions based

00:11:08.653 --> 00:11:10.178
on how easy the work will be?

00:11:10.178 --> 00:11:12.654
I mean, I remember in
college they would give you

00:11:12.654 --> 00:11:14.648
this book where all
the students would rate

00:11:14.648 --> 00:11:16.251
the classes and the would rate things like

00:11:16.251 --> 00:11:19.973
how easy the class was,
and how much they liked

00:11:19.973 --> 00:11:21.140
the professor.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:24.251
And the first year I
picked all my classes based

00:11:24.251 --> 00:11:28.691
on workload, and I picked
everything a low workload.

00:11:28.691 --> 00:11:32.457
And pretty bored, didn't
work very hard, which

00:11:32.457 --> 00:11:35.979
was fine, but nothing
was dynamic and nothing

00:11:35.979 --> 00:11:37.319
really excited me.

00:11:37.319 --> 00:11:39.579
And I, thank goodness,
learned that and so the

00:11:39.579 --> 00:11:42.302
second year I picked all
my classes by professor

00:11:42.302 --> 00:11:44.624
rating, regardless of the workload.

00:11:44.624 --> 00:11:46.947
So every class I had, I
had these dynamic, amazing,

00:11:46.947 --> 00:11:49.919
incredible human beings
passing on their knowledge

00:11:49.919 --> 00:11:53.568
and you were excited
to work hard for them.

00:11:53.568 --> 00:11:55.947
And so again, the question
is, what are the filters

00:11:55.947 --> 00:11:56.787
we're using?

00:11:56.787 --> 00:11:59.060
So if you're only chasing
the mighty dollar,

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.166
then you will have jobs that will pay you

00:12:01.166 --> 00:12:02.435
a little more than the last, but

00:12:02.435 --> 00:12:04.083
are you enjoying yourself?

00:12:04.083 --> 00:12:05.652
And I talked to a guy
recently, who was in,

00:12:05.652 --> 00:12:07.208
he's in bad shape.

00:12:07.208 --> 00:12:10.037
He really hates his life
and he's really depressed

00:12:10.037 --> 00:12:11.347
and he doesn't know what to do.

00:12:11.347 --> 00:12:12.854
And so we're going
through all his old jobs

00:12:12.854 --> 00:12:14.786
and I said, give me a
job that you've loved.

00:12:14.786 --> 00:12:15.620
And he hadn't.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.401
Every single job he's
chosen out of college,

00:12:17.401 --> 00:12:19.641
he picked because of the
money and if something

00:12:19.641 --> 00:12:23.882
offered him more somewhere
else, he took it, regardless.

00:12:23.882 --> 00:12:27.004
And the amazing thing is, he plateaued.

00:12:27.004 --> 00:12:29.913
Because if you're only chasing
the result, if you're only

00:12:29.913 --> 00:12:33.549
chasing the thing that
makes it easy, right, then

00:12:33.549 --> 00:12:35.762
eventually you will get
bored or they'll get bored

00:12:35.762 --> 00:12:38.216
of you, and you plateau.

00:12:38.216 --> 00:12:40.101
In other words, chasing
the almighty dollar,

00:12:40.101 --> 00:12:42.788
if that's your only thing,
it eventually flattens out.

00:12:42.788 --> 00:12:44.665
Whereas if you're chasing
the thing that excites you,

00:12:44.665 --> 00:12:47.072
the human beings to be around,
the work that excites you,

00:12:47.072 --> 00:12:51.239
the stuff that, you know,
you can get passionate about.

00:12:53.213 --> 00:12:56.926
The irony is that you'll
actually make way, way more.

00:12:56.926 --> 00:12:58.571
Because you're excited
and they appreciate your

00:12:58.571 --> 00:12:59.920
excitement and they reward
your excitement and you're

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.230
better at your work because
you want to work harder

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.368
and all that stuff.

00:13:03.368 --> 00:13:06.477
You don't have to strain to work harder.

00:13:06.477 --> 00:13:09.845
So decision-making is
simply a matter of filters.

00:13:09.845 --> 00:13:11.355
And so I've made decisions
in my life that I

00:13:11.355 --> 00:13:13.084
would rather be happy than right.

00:13:13.084 --> 00:13:15.834
I'd rather do good than get rich.

00:13:17.139 --> 00:13:21.060
And so the decisions I make
put me in positions where,

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.501
when I leave any engagement,
when I leave any meeting,

00:13:23.501 --> 00:13:25.918
I feel that I've contributed.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.326
Rare are the times anymore
when you walk around

00:13:29.326 --> 00:13:31.256
going, just think of the
money, just think of the money,

00:13:31.256 --> 00:13:33.084
think of the money, you know.

00:13:33.084 --> 00:13:35.728
Because that doesn't feel nice.

00:13:35.728 --> 00:13:37.595
And the experience I have, I don't enjoy

00:13:37.595 --> 00:13:39.612
traveling to them and I
don't enjoy traveling home.

00:13:39.612 --> 00:13:40.711
Where if I have an
amazing experience, I am

00:13:40.711 --> 00:13:42.363
looking forward to getting
there and I'm excited

00:13:42.363 --> 00:13:43.446
when I leave.

00:13:44.326 --> 00:13:46.759
So it's just decision, decision-making is

00:13:46.759 --> 00:13:48.981
just a matter of what
filters you use and if

00:13:48.981 --> 00:13:51.140
you're good about keeping
those filters up and

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.651
clear, then make your decision.

00:13:53.651 --> 00:13:56.922
I don't judge anybody
by how, if they choose

00:13:56.922 --> 00:13:58.640
to use different filters.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:01.910
These are just the filters
I choose to live my life.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:04.944
Not right or wrong, just
those are my decisions.

00:14:04.944 --> 00:14:06.247
That's my filter.

